      "content": "Sophisticated libertarian arguments move beyond simplistic theft claims by appealing to the Lockean concept of self-ownership and justly acquired property. They maintain that an individual has impregnable ownership over their self and the fruits of their labor, making any mandatory redistribution beyond the non-aggression principle illegitimate. From this viewpoint, state intervention, even in the name of welfare, violates these inherent natural rights by compelling individuals to surrender their uncoerced holdings to achieve a socially desirable outcome. This places a high moral barrier on state power, rooting it solely in consent and the protection of individual spheres.",
